  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-14> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-14--gpt> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-14--gpt> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch03-14: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.58" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.582"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.72"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Range edges and climate are measurable at broad scale, but competition usually must be inferred rather than observed. Existing data permit strong tests for selected taxa and regions, not the claim's near-universal scope." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For many species, model range-edge occupancy or demographic performance against climate suitability and competitor occurrence or removal. The claim is supported if biotic limitation commonly dominates except at the harshest physiological limits, and refuted if climate alone commonly determines edges." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Occurrence records do not directly identify why populations fail beyond a range edge.", "Biotic interactions and physiological limits are sparsely measured across taxa." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-14--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-14--gpt--dataset-2> .
